r","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T10:43:26-08:00","id":17802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=17733#post17733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You and me, both. People talk about which one is &quot;their&quot; Doctor, well, he was mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's the Doctor I grew up with. I got my girlfriend into Dr. Who, but unfortunately it was during the reign of Tennant (I like him, but he's no Baker).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T11:25:20-08:00","id":17825,"title":"","content":"Minorly spoilerish stuff: I\u2019m relatively new to Doctor Who, and this is the first multi-Doctor story I\u2019ve seen. Is that bit about \u201cour timelines have crossed, so they\u2019re a bit unstable, so you younger versions of me won\u2019t remember any of this when it\u2019s over\u201d something that\u2019s happened before? It seems like a useful technique for enabling \u201ctalking with yourself\u201d scenes that aren\u2019t fundamentally disruptive: by the time the Doctor\u2019s timeline wraps around to the older version entering the conversation, he\u2019ll have forgotten all but the most basic facts about the meeting and can approach it as if it was happening for the first time. (Oh, and I loved the War Doctor\u2019s reaction to the \u201cTimey-Wimey\u201d line. I\u2019ve always wanted someone to call the Doctor out on that bit.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T13:14:50-08:00","id":17886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=17825#post17825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minorly spoilerish stuff: I\u2019m relatively new to Doctor Who, and this is the first multi-Doctor story I\u2019ve seen. Is that bit about \u201cour timelines have crossed, so they\u2019re a bit unstable, so you younger versions of me won\u2019t remember any of this when it\u2019s over\u201d something that\u2019s happened before? It seems like a useful technique for enabling \u201ctalking with yourself\u201d scenes that aren\u2019t fundamentally disruptive: by the time the Doctor\u2019s timeline wraps around to the older version entering the conversation, he\u2019ll have forgotten all but the most basic facts about the meeting and can approach it as if it was happening for the first time. (Oh, and I loved the War Doctor\u2019s reaction to the \u201cTimey-Wimey\u201d line. I\u2019ve always wanted someone to call the Doctor out on that bit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a gag short between 10 and 5 a few years back where 10 remembers how to solve the paradox because he saw 10 do it back when he was 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T15:32:18-08:00","id":17973,"title":"","content":"Yeah there's been other multi-Doctor stories, most notably the 10th and 20th Anniversary specials, The Three Doctors and The Five Doctors respectively* and they have the same general thing. Actually the 11th Doctor had some inkling of what was going on at the beginning while in those older stories the oldest Doctor present had no idea what was going on. At least if I'm remembering it correctly, it's been a while since I've seen them.<br /> <br /> *It's kind of a bad name for both specials as they both were largely short a Doctor. In the Three Doctors the 1st Doctor only appeared on a screen a couple of times to talk to his future selves which was because William Hartnell (the 1st Doctor) was old and in terrible health and couldn't really handle a more hands-on role. In the Five Doctors the 4th Doctor only appeared in a clip from an unaired episode as Tom Baker, the longest running Doctor, felt that it was too soon since his departure for him to return. Which he later regretted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T21:42:29-08:00","id":18162,"title":"","content":"All I can say that it was GREAT!!!! I watched it both times (Bo, Elisabeth's dad was going who is recording this). He did his JFK conspiracy theories...I tried not to squeal like a little girl. I just LOVE it when Peter's (13) eyes showed up. I cried when Tom came out as the Curator... Billie played the best ghosty Companion, making John Hurt think of another way that can work, not destroy the planet.<br /> <br /> Then an episode came on where Saxon was revived. Talk about twists and turns...and Timothy Dalton...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T21:55:35-08:00","id":18170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=17886#post17886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was a gag short between 10 and 5 a few years back where 10 remembers how to solve the paradox because he saw 10 do it back when he was 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>But note that 5 *wasn't expecting* 10 to remember that, and was actually surprised that he did! <br /> <br /> It's never been stated, but my working theory was always that the Laws of Time enact a kind of amnesia on Time Lords who cross paths with themselves this way; it only makes sense, otherwise in the Five Doctors, they all would have known who the actual villain was from the Second Doctor on! Once they leave, the oldest Doctor present (5, in the case of TFD) suddenly finds that he can remember the adventure from all POVs involved. DotD came pretty close to confirming this theory by the end (10 remembers what happens in Time Crash because of the unstable nature of the temporal anomoly that brought him together with 5). <br /> <br /> One wonders how the story might have been different if Eccleston, the 9th Doctor, had signed on. Maybe he didn't because it retconned the numbering of the Doctors, and he was revealed to be the 10th all along? I'm still waiting for the fandom to split in two once that revelation really sinks in... Hm, wonder if they would have called it &quot;The Four Doctors&quot;?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T21:58:28-08:00","id":18171,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I found a link to &quot;The Five(ish) Doctors Reboot&quot;. Absolutely hysterical, and I don't think it's just because I'm a long-time whovian who gets some of the more obscure references! John Barrowman's part had me in stitches, and there are some VERY surprising cameos:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p01m3kfy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/1200x675/p01m3kfw.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p01m3kfy\" target=\"_blank\"> BBC One - Doctor Who (2005&ndash;2022), The Day of the Doctor, The Five(ish) Doctors Reboot </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p01m3kfy\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p01m3kfy </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A star studded special written and directed by Peter Davison. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T01:00:10-08:00","id":18257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=16925#post16925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted the Time War to have a bunch more reality-fuckery, but it was the most fun I've had watching Doctor Who in a while. The reveal of number 13 was also pretty epic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given some of the vague descriptions we've gotten, I'm don't think it would be possible to show some of the most extreme weapons and phenomena on either side without it being a letdown. It just wouldn't be possible to live up to the hype. (although the current Doctor Who RPG has a supplement that touches on the subject briefly, if you <i>really</i> need to know more about Time War shenanigans)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T12:47:22-08:00","id":18637,"title":"","content":"That, and didn't the ep explicitely state near the beginning that they'd already used up their &quot;reality fuckery&quot; arsenal, except the Moment? The 8th Doc novels have some damned impressive high-concept weapons used in the first Time War against The Enemy (before the Time War that the new series introduced), so you might want to check those out, too.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm hoping that the 12th Doctor has to go up against some of the Dalek-allied horrors that may have survived, such as the Nightmare Child...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T13:01:45-08:00","id":18652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=18257#post18257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given some of the vague descriptions we've gotten, I'm don't think it would be possible to show some of the most extreme weapons and phenomena on either side without it being a letdown. It just wouldn't be possible to live up to the hype. (although the current Doctor Who RPG has a supplement that touches on the subject briefly, if you <i>really</i> need to know more about Time War shenanigans)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, one of the things about Doctor Who is that <i>showing </i>doesn't work nearly as well as <i>implying</i> because it's often just <b>too big</b> to show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T13:23:36-08:00","id":18671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=18652#post18652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, one of the things about Doctor Who is that <i>showing </i>doesn't work nearly as well as <i>implying</i> because it's often just <b>too big</b> to show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like the primordials in Exalted then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/327-drecain","name":"Drecain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T13:24:41-08:00","id":18672,"title":"","content":"Mmm...that was certainly true of the classic show, with its Special Effects Failures it's famous for...<br /> <br /> But effects have progressed to the point that the imagination is pretty much the limit, even for television. Just because no show that I can think of has escalated on-screen action to the &quot;exploding galaxies&quot; level found in pulp sci-fi, doesn't mean that it can't be done, and done well. Just that no one has the guts/vision to TRY, so far...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T13:41:49-08:00","id":18685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=18672#post18672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm...that was certainly true of the classic show, with its Special Effects Failures it's famous for...<br /> <br /> But effects have progressed to the point that the imagination is pretty much the limit, even for television. Just because no show that I can think of has escalated on-screen action to the &quot;exploding galaxies&quot; level found in pulp sci-fi, doesn't mean that it can't be done, and done well. Just that no one has the guts/vision to TRY, so far...</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if my imagination of the end of time doesn't match yours? It's the same old problem visual media has always had - mass appeal doesn't always appeal to <i>all </i>the masses. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T15:30:59-08:00","id":18766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=18637#post18637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and didn't the ep explicitely state near the beginning that they'd already used up their &quot;reality fuckery&quot; arsenal, except the Moment? The 8th Doc novels have some damned impressive high-concept weapons used in the first Time War against The Enemy (before the Time War that the new series introduced), so you might want to check those out, too.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm hoping that the 12th Doctor has to go up against some of the Dalek-allied horrors that may have survived, such as the Nightmare Child...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I've always seen the Horde of Travesties, the Nightmare Child, the Could-Have-Been-King and his army of Meanwhiles and Never-weres as Cthulhu-esque entities, the kinds of horrors that the mere sight of which drives men mad. Well at least lower species like humans. Same with the majority of the Last Great Time War. Hence revealing them to us would ultimately cheapen that for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T07:11:17-08:00","id":19155,"title":"","content":"So, unrelated, but can someone help me out on this one...<br /> <br /> I've seen (I think) all the 10th Doctor random episodes (Waters of Mars, Planet of the Dead, End of Time). The end of End of Time had Ten running around to do last visits with all the companions he had before he goes and this part confuses me - when the hell did Mickey and Martha hook up and go off to fight Sontarians with frickin' laser beams?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T08:10:16-08:00","id":19186,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Lox, I'm glad I'm not the only one who saw the Time Lord soldiers using laser rifles and said &quot;Really? That's the best they got?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T09:18:18-08:00","id":19216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=19155#post19155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, unrelated, but can someone help me out on this one...<br /> <br /> I've seen (I think) all the 10th Doctor random episodes (Waters of Mars, Planet of the Dead, End of Time). The end of End of Time had Ten running around to do last visits with all the companions he had before he goes and this part confuses me - when the hell did Mickey and Martha hook up and go off to fight Sontarians with frickin' laser beams?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They never really explained that beyond the end of Stolen Earth where the two of them leave together. Presumably they started working together for UNIT or Torchwood, fell in love and got married.<br /> <br /> Lox:And that's exactly why I didn't see it at theatres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T18:02:55-08:00","id":19471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also delayed watching it, to see it in a theater monday night.<br /> <br /> Never. Again.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Lox, the tiny popcorn screams!<br /> <br /> More seriously, the people were something I enjoyed. It does suck that you missed the curator's lines, but the energy and general feeling of community from people sharing a fandom really ramped up the experience for me.<br /> <br /> Also, the clapping is more of a solidarity thing. People aren't clapping because they think the movie can hear them; they get to participate in a conversation with the rest of the crowd that ultimately amounts to, &quot;I thought it was awesome too!&quot; because the language of clapping is fairly simple.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T19:21:32-08:00","id":19491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sparketh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=19471#post19471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Lox, the tiny popcorn screams!<br /> <br /> More seriously, the people were something I enjoyed. It does suck that you missed the curator's lines, but the energy and general feeling of community from people sharing a fandom really ramped up the experience for me.<br /> <br /> Also, the clapping is more of a solidarity thing. People aren't clapping because they think the movie can hear them; they get to participate in a conversation with the rest of the crowd that ultimately amounts to, &quot;I thought it was awesome too!&quot; because the language of clapping is fairly simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>unfortunately it's a case of so much communication that it drowns out the source completely.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, that level of participation and excitement is fine... If you're talking about something like the Rocky Horror Picture Show, where it's not something people are trying to watch for the movie but instead are specifically there for the crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T03:37:13-08:00","id":21097,"title":"","content":"So who else thinks Sean Pertwee would make a great Doctor? He's the son of Jon Pertwee, the third Doctor, and played Sgt. Wells in Dog Soldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T04:11:01-08:00","id":21102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/16650-the-doctor-is-in?p=21097#post21097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So who else thinks Sean Pertwee would make a great Doctor? He's the son of Jon Pertwee, the third Doctor, and played Sgt. Wells in Dog Soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I could see Sean Pertwee playing the Master!<br /> I think it's his eyes and that slightly otherworldly gravelly voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T00:35:56-08:00","id":22999,"title":"","content":"As much as I enjoyed Simm's performance, I'm definitely ready for a new Master. I don't have anyone in particular in mind, but I've always wanted to see a different take on the &quot;obviously evil&quot; role he's been given...The &quot;charasmatic politician&quot; was a great way to go, but maybe he could be a seemingly innocent guy, all dressed in white for a change, something like a personable religious leader...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:34:21-08:00","id":23075,"title":"","content":"Honestly I doubt we'll being seeing the Master again for a while, probably not until Gallifrey is found which I have a feeling will take awhile.<br /> <br /> And we've got our first teaser for the Christmas Special.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DMOOLd_44Mo\" data-code=\"DMOOLd_44Mo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/DMOOLd_44Mo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T19:37:27-08:00","id":37110,"title":"","content":"Just finished watching <i>The Time of the Doctor</i> and wow... Not only did they address the issue of how many regenerations he had left* but they gave the 11th a truly great send off.<br /> <br /> *The issue created by the existence of the Meta-Crisis Doctor and the War Doctor.<br /> <br /> Farewell Matt Smith, you were one of my favorite Doctors and I will miss you.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And welcome Peter Capaldi, you have some big shoes to fill but I have a feeling you'll be alright.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T20:28:20-08:00","id":37129,"title":"","content":"I wish I knew where to start, because the appeal of Doctor Who has so completely eluded me in the past. Where do I start? Where should I start? Is there some reading I need to do prior to starting it?<br /> <br /> One of the accusations I've heard levelled against it is that it's really &quot;british humor&quot; which I think I understand what that means, but I'm wondering if that's actually the case? Obviously others are very much capable of &quot;getting it&quot; and enjoying it, so it's not as if no one else can enjoy that humor.<br /> <br /> I just couldn't get hooked the first time I tried, I think it was with Eccleston?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T21:08:36-08:00","id":37140,"title":"","content":"Oh I don't know about 'British humor'. Certainly there are references sprinkled here and there that people in other parts of the world won't get but they aren't all that common or even all that noticeable. Besides the humor is just one small part of what makes Doctor Who awesome.<br /> <br /> Eccleston was the Ninth Doctor, the first of Doctors following the restart of the series.<br /> <br /> Best advice I can give you is to pick a Doctor (or several) and start watching their episodes. Each incarnation of the Doctor, each actor who has played the Doctor has brought something to the role to make their version memorable. Of course by the same token not everyone likes all the incarnations of the Doctor. Personally I love them all though if I had to list my top five, in no particular order, they would be the First Doctor, the Third, the Fourth, the Seventh and the Eleventh.<br /> <br /> Not to long ago a couple of my friends came to me asking about what episodes of the old series are worth watching so I've been slowly putting together a list of episodes for them. At the moment I only have the first three Doctors as the Fourth was the longest running Doctor so there's a <i>lot</i> of episodes to sift through.<br /> <br /> Though you could look for <a href=\"http://tardis.wikia.com/wiki/The_Doctors_Revisited\" target=\"_blank\">The Doctor Revisited</a>, a series created as part of the lead up to the recent 50th Anniversary. Each episode starts off talking about that particular incarnation of the Doctor, the companions he traveled with, the famous foes he fought and some of the memorable moments which is then followed up by one of the better episodes of that Doctor. Failing that, find and watch the episode shown with that Doctor in the series. I know for a fact you can find the episodes of the old series (Doctors 1-7 and movie of 8) on the website DailyMotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"ht